directs use of local Feishu credentials, external file transfer, runtime package installation, and unsafe document conversion settings.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill runs local converters and uses wkhtmltopdf with local-file access enabled or Chromium with --no-sandbox while spreadsheet and CLI text are interpolated into HTML without escaping.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The Python script installs openpyxl and markdownify at runtime with unpinned pip commands, creating mutable and unaudited supply-chain behavior during normal report processing.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"SKILL.md instructs agents to read Feishu app credentials from openclaw.json, use raw Feishu API calls to download files, and upload/send generated reports without clear user confirmation, recipient scoping, or local-only default.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No backdoor, scheduled task, or privilege escalation was found, but runtime pip installs can persist changes in the Python environment and the Feishu credential workflow grants high-impact account access.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Core report generation from Excel is coherent with the finance-analysis purpose, but the skill advertises PDF/CSV/Feishu-doc/ticker inputs that the shipped script does not implement and handles likely sensitive financial data.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Use this only in an isolated environment with pinned dependencies, avoid processing untrusted spreadsheets, prefer local HTML output, and require explicit approval before any Feishu credential use, file download, report upload, or message send.","findings":"[TP4] unexpected: Confirmed that the description overstates supported inputs and triggers; the implementation accepts a local Excel workbook path and does not implement PDF, CSV, ticker lookup, or Feishu document parsing.\n[SC2] expected: The cited curl commands are Feishu API calls, not remote script execution, so the external-script claim is overstated; the same evidence still matters because it uses raw authenticated network access.\n[SSD-3] expected: Confirmed the instructions tell the agent to read Feishu appId/appSecret from openclaw.json and use them for file retrieval and delivery, which is high-impact and under-scoped for sensitive finance documents.\n[AST5] unexpected: Confirmed os.system pip installs for openpyxl and markdownify; installing unpinned packages during report generation is not necessary or proportionate.\n[SQP-2] expected: Confirmed optional online benchmarking and Feishu upload/download flows, but the docs do not clearly warn what sensitive financial data or generated reports may leave the local environment.\n[LP3] unexpected: Confirmed the skill relies on broad shell, file, and network instructions without an explicit least-privilege boundary or safer scoped connector flow.\n[SDI-2] expected: Confirmed direct Feishu credential use and report upload instructions; delivery is related to the stated integration, but it lacks explicit consent and destination validation.\n[E1] expected: Confirmed external Feishu transmission paths for file upload and message sending; this is disclosed as a workflow step but risky for confidential reports without clear user control.\n[SQP-3] expected: The Chinese-language documentation and output appear consistent with the examples and target finance-report format, so this is a usability/localization note rather than a security driver.\n[AST4] expected: Subprocess use for PDF/DOCX/Markdown conversion is expected, but the local-file-access and no-sandbox flags combined with unescaped workbook content make the implementation materially unsafe for untrusted inputs.\n[T08] unexpected: Accepted the static-scan concern: runtime unpinned dependency installation creates avoidable supply-chain and environment-mutation risk.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted the static-scan concern: unescaped spreadsheet and CLI content can reach generated HTML that is then processed by weakened document renderers.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789114016565}}}}}